-      round trip with the controller's own bytes printed; then an
-      inquiry, and a named refusal for pairing (out of scope here).
-- [ ] **Wi-Fi:** promote the virtual AP from a self-test to a **data
-      path**: `wifi_virt` frames reach the IP stack (the LLC/SNAP path
-      already carries 78 bytes at T6), so `ping` over the virtual AP is
-      a real receipt; the real-chip backend stays RES-61's M half.
-- [ ] The two status.md rows keep 🚧 and cite the split explicitly
-      (protocol ✅ / silicon M) instead of implying nothing works.
-
-**Definition of done:** new `test_bt_dongle.sh` green with the
-controller's BD_ADDR; `test_wifi_virtual_ap` promoted to assert an
-end-to-end echo; RES-61 records the metal remainder.
